  "content": {
    "equation": "Z_Score = ((Length/M)L - 1) / (L * S)\nPercentile = ZtoPercentile(Z_Score)",
    "notes": [
      "This calculator uses measured recumbent Length for infants and toddlers from birth through 36 months of age.",
      "It is not valid for standing height.",
      "At the extremes (>97th percentile or <3rd percentile), small differences in percentiles represent clinically important differences. At these extremes, the Z-score is a more precise reflection of how far the measurement deviates from the mean and is a useful tool for tracking changes.",
      "LMS data used in this calculator are shown in the data table below.",
      "For all LMS tables, the row in the table corresponding to the patient-specific value is found in the first column of the table; values to be used for L (the Box-Cox power), M (the median), and the first column of the table; values to be used for L (the Box-Cox power), M (the median), and S (the generalized coefficient of variation) in the equation for Z-score are retrieved.",
      "Z-scores may be used to do a table lookup for the corresponding percentile in the Normal table percentiles for Z-score table (below). Numbers along the left side (Y-axis) of the table represent the first number and first decimal place of the Z-score, while the numbers along the top (X-axis) of the table represent the second decimal position of the Z-score."
    ],
    "conditional_notes": null,
    "calc_details": null,
    "data_input_disclaimer": "ONLY DIGITS 0 TO 9 AND A SINGLE DECIMAL POINT (\".\") ARE ACCEPTABLE AS NUMERIC INPUTS. ATTEMPTED INPUT OF OTHER CHARACTERS INTO A NUMERIC FIELD MAY LEAD TO AN INCORRECT RESULT.",
